<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Tullow sells Czech assets for 2.1 mln stg.</title>
<headline>Tullow sells Czech assets for 2.1 mln stg.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Irish group Tullow Oil Plc said on Thursday it sold its production and exploration interests in the Czech Republic to Medusa Oil &amp; Gas Ltd for 2.1 million stg in cash.</p>
<p>As a result, Tullow said it would not inject the assets into Medusa Petroleum Plc, a company in which it would have had a 25 percent stake.</p>
<p>Tullow said it would use the cash, as well as 1.0 million stg it had planned to contribute to Medusa Petroleum, toward other projects in India and Africa.</p>
<p>-- Dublin Newsroom +353 1 676 9775</p>
</text>
